Z||000000||general||04-27-2000||01:03 AM||||    I have been dealing with a problem pertaining to my temperature guage coolant sensor/sending unit.After checking the wiring to my temp guage it seems that my problem is in my sending unit.I have replaced the sending unit once already and am preparing to do it again.I once saw a reply on this forum where theogre posted a listing of specs on sensors under the heading HOW TO:MAT & COOLANT SENSORS ,It stated that the coolant sensor should have about 1800 ohms resistance at 100 deg.F and about 185 ohms resistance at 210 deg.F . My question is should the measurement be taken across the 2 terminals or should this be done with the sensor installed and the ohmeter connected at some other point in the wiring with the ignition on? Any thoughts ???||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-27-2000||01:11 AM||||I just went thru this myself. You measure from 1 pin to the case. (if installed in block anywhere on block is fine) One pin will read ohms as stated in your thread the other will by an open. The reason is one pin goes to gage and the other pin is for the temp light. ||||reg||1
